<head>
    <title>Quick Start | Nijor</title>
</head>
<body layout="docs">
    <section>
        <h1>Quick Start</h1>
        <p>This guide will help you create and run your first Nijor project.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h1>Install the CLI</h1>
        <p>
            In order to use Nijor, make sure you have Bun installed (Node will also work). <br>
            Install Nijor globally :
        </p>
    <code lang="shell" shiki>
        bun add nijor -g
    </code>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h1>Create a project</h1>
    <code lang="shell" shiki>
        nijor create my-app
    </code>

    <code lang="shell" shiki>
        cd my-app
    </code>
        <p>A Nijor project is created with many files and folders.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h1>Start the dev server</h1>
    <code lang="shell" shiki>
        nijor dev
    </code>
        <p>The dev server will start on port 3000 with <span class="txt">live_reload</span> enabled. You can change this behavior in the <span class="txt">nijor.config.js</span>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h1>Build for production</h1>
        <p>
            When you're ready to deploy your app, you can create an optimized production build:
        </p>
    <code lang="shell" shiki>
        nijor build
    </code>
        <p>
            This will generate a production-ready version of your app with optimized assets.
        </p>
    </section>
</body>